      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the original test. The key issues are:\n1. Lots of dead code (unused helper methods, broken abstract method signatures with non-existent type `T`)\n2. Unused imports\n3. The comment in the test is cryptic\n\nI'll write a clean, minimal version with only what's needed for the single test method.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all dead code (unused helper methods, broken generic type references, and unused imports), keeps only the `createEmptyFilter` and `getTestShape` helpers needed by the single test method, and adds a clear Javadoc explaining the SparseBloomFilter's TreeSet-based behavior and why the merge-with-nothing scenario should leave the filter empty."
